skillful|showing-ability|ADJECTIVE|showing practiced ability|Able to do something well through knowledge or practice, or showing that ability.|khéo léo; có kỹ năng|The skillful carpenter repaired the chair without changing its shape.|Người thợ mộc khéo léo sửa chiếc ghế mà không làm thay đổi hình dạng của nó.|Skillful at doing something; skillful is usual American spelling, skilful usual British spelling.|-
word|unit-of-language|NOUN|unit of language|A unit of language that carries meaning and can be spoken or written.|từ; từ ngữ|The teacher wrote each new word beside a small drawing.|Giáo viên viết từng từ mới bên cạnh một hình vẽ nhỏ.|Countable; a word, words; a word for something. This definition does not require every word to have spaces around it.|0
amazed|very-surprised|ADJECTIVE|very surprised|Very surprised by something unexpected or impressive.|kinh ngạc; rất ngạc nhiên|We were amazed at the detail in the tiny wooden model.|Chúng tôi kinh ngạc trước những chi tiết trong mô hình gỗ nhỏ xíu.|Amazed at or by something; amazed to do, amazed that. Amazing describes the cause.|0
freight|transported-goods|NOUN|goods carried for transport|Goods transported in large quantities, especially by ship, train or truck.|hàng hóa vận tải|The train carried freight overnight while passenger services had stopped.|Đoàn tàu chở hàng hóa qua đêm trong khi các chuyến chở khách đã ngừng.|Uncountable; freight transport, a freight train. Cargo overlaps in meaning, but neither word creates a canonical identity claim.|-
logical|following-sound-reasoning|ADJECTIVE|following clear reasoning|Following a clear and consistent line of reasoning.|hợp lý; có logic|Her explanation gave a logical reason for changing the timetable.|Lời giải thích của cô đưa ra lý do hợp lý cho việc đổi thời gian biểu.|A logical argument or conclusion; logical does not by itself guarantee that every starting assumption is true.|0
